     notes: ﻿# Rooftop Scout, California Roofer Guru, 2026-11-24. Model estimates from public records, not inspections: a status is a probability. | # Score: chance of at least one paid roofing job (a replacement or tile relay within five years, a repair call within twelve months, or wind, hail or fire damage still open). Green at 26 or more, orange at 19. | # p_roofer_15yr, p_replaced_15yr, p_wind_15yr, p_leak_15yr, p_fire_15yr, likely_damage_15yr: the 15 year outlook, the chance of any roofing job, of a replacement and of each kind of damage by 2041 if the years bring weather and fire at the pace of the ZIP's record (gust days, rain and atmospheric rivers, CAL FIRE's losses 2013 to 2025), for the roof's likely age and covering (without the roof's own heat). Odds from records and stated judgments, not a forecast of a storm or a fire. | # Sources: FEMA USA Structures; county assessors' public parcel layers; re-roof permits of the City and County of Los Angeles, San Francisco, Sacramento and San Jose; CAL FIRE Fire Hazard Severity Zones, fire perimeters and damage inspections; the atlas's hazard columns (CW3E, NOAA, ASCE) and roof age model (module 17). Street View links open Google Maps. | # Terrain columns: ground elevation from AWS Terrain Tiles (zoom 14, over the USGS 10 m model) or, where a tile was not in hand, from the statewide 1 km grid (see elev_source); site slope and aspect across 30 m each way; terrain_position compares the point with the ground 300 m around it; province from
